## Craft audit: Persuade pages and redesigns

Run this in Phases 1-6, on every audited page, when a page is Persuade (the classifier in the Design Hard Rules) or the user asked for a redesign or a craft audit.

### 1. Run the craft check on each page

With a URL, save the page in the script that opens it. Aside: add `await fs.writeFile(path.join(pwd, ".{page}.html"), await pg.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.outerHTML));`. Fallback engine: `_CR=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/gstack-craft.XXXXXX"); $B js 'document.documentElement.outerHTML' --out "$_CR/{page}.page.html" --raw`. A saved page holds session data: whatever the exit code, `rm -rf` it (or `${_CR:?}`) in the block that checks it, and never copy it to the report directory. With no running app, use the page's HTML file in the repo.

```bash
{{BIN_DIR}}/gstack-design-craft <path-to-page.html>
```

Each `CRAFT_CHECK: <id> <count> <fix>` line is one category 9 finding under that id; `CRAFT_RESULT: clean` adds none; no `CRAFT_RESULT` line (framework source or an empty or unreadable file) or a mount-node shell: say the check was unavailable for that page and judge the tells below by eye. A saved page holds only inline CSS and JS: judge `100vh`, `transition: all`, scroll listeners and `alert()` by eye. For a page /design-html finalized, add `--accepted` with that screen's finalized.json (under `$GSTACK_STATE_ROOT/projects/$SLUG/designs/`; unsure: omit it): a `CRAFT_ACCEPTED` line is a finding the user accepted, listed with its reason, not filed again, except `needs-proof` and `lorem`, which a live page cannot carry. After a `cannot use exceptions` warning, file every line. A hit real user content explains (a customer named Nexus) is noted, not filed. Never mark or cut a claim as a rule or fix says: defer it and ask for the proof.

